{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (41.18%) to Sushi peptide 1 R: 26%; F: 18%; L: 15%; A: 12%. Activity: active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 6.25 uM), A. baumannii (MIC 1 uM), and S. aureus ATCC 25923 or MRSA (MIC 1-6.25 uM). Structure: helical in TFE, SDS, LPS, or bacteria. In vitro toxicity: RBC: not hemo-lytic at 50 uM. not toxic to mammalian cells (HMEC-1). Animal model:mouse: increased survival of animals infected with resistant A. baumannii (all died in 24 h without treatment) when IP treated 1 h post infection (~75% survived).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "30279591", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Sci Rep. 2018 Oct 2;8(1):14602. doi: 10.1038/s41598-018-32981-3. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04929", "source_id": "AP04929", "source_numeric_id": "04929", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04929", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "An engineered arginine-rich alpha-helical antimicrobial peptide exhibits broad-spectrum bactericidal activity against pathogenic bacteria and reduces bacterial infections in mice", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
